authmgr: validate alg, iss, aud, exp/nbf and email of bearer (OIDC) tokens

Apply with `patch -p1` on gromox-3.13 (8b620206). AGPL-3.0-or-later, same as gromox.

verify_token() only checked the RS256 signature and "exp". Any token signed
by the realm key was accepted for any mailbox named in its "email" claim,
including tokens issued to a different OAuth client (audience confusion).

- JOSE header must have alg == "RS256" (the only algorithm implemented).
- "exp" must be present, integral and in the future; "nbf" (if present) passed.
- "email" must be a non-empty string.
- New gromox.cfg directives bearer_issuer and bearer_audience (default empty
  = unchanged behaviour, with a NOTICE in the log): "iss" must equal the
  issuer; the audience must equal "aud" or be an element of it.
- The claim logic is a header-only function (include/gromox/bearer.hpp) with
  a unit test (tests/bearer.cpp, part of `make check`).

Tested (docs/status/sso-rollout-results.md): unit test 27/27; real Keycloak
tokens through zcore mapi_logon_token with different policies
(blueprints/lab/tests/gromox_bearer_claims_test.sh).

