+\fBbearer_issuer\fP
+Required value of the \fBiss\fP claim of OIDC bearer tokens (JWT) that are
+presented for login (e.g. by grommunio-web with Keycloak, see
+\fB/etc/gromox/bearer_pubkey\fP). When empty, the issuer is not checked.
+.br
+Default: (empty)
+.TP
+\fBbearer_audience\fP
+Value that must be contained in the \fBaud\fP claim of bearer tokens (string,
+or one element of an array). Without this, any token signed by the issuer's
+key is accepted, including tokens that were issued to a different
+application. Setting both \fBbearer_issuer\fP and \fBbearer_audience\fP is
+recommended. Independent of these settings, bearer tokens are only accepted
+when the JOSE header has \fBalg\fP=\fBRS256\fP, when \fBexp\fP is present and
+in the future, \fBnbf\fP (if present) has passed, and \fBemail\fP is non-empty.
+.br
+Default: (empty)
+.TP
 \fBauth_backend_selection\fP
 This controls how authmgr will verify passwords supplied with login operations.
 See the "Authentication modes" section below for details.
